{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>פרא אדם.</b> Free among men, like the sense of \"Who sent the wild ass free?\" (Job 39:5). The meaning is that no stranger from his family will rule over him. Some say: פרא and אדם, like שמש ירח עמד זבולה (Habakkuk 3:11) — because he is a פרא, his hand is against all; and because he is אדם, everyone's hand is against him. The correct view in my eyes is that among men he is like a wild ass: he overpowers everything by his strength, and afterward everyone's hand is against him. So too it is explicit in Daniel, for it is the fourth beast." "<b>ועל פני כל אחיו.</b> They are the sons of Keturah. And so it is written: על פני כל אחיו נפל (Genesis 25:18). And likewise the Midianites, from the sons of Keturah, are called Ishmaelites in the Torah and in the book of Judges."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:49.535972626Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}